\DOC LOCAL_EPDOUBLE_SAFETY_TAC

\TYPE {LOCAL_EPDOUBLE_SAFETY_TAC : string -> int -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Applies a named subroutine-specification assumption to the current {eventually}
goal, advancing the symbolic state from step {n-1} to step {n} and replacing
the old state's assumptions with ones describing the state after the call.

\DESCRIBE
{assump_name : string} is the label of an assumption in the goal that holds the
universally quantified {ensures} specification of the called subroutine;
{n : int} is the index of the new symbolic state, i.e. the name of the state
variable referred to by the resulting goal's {eventually} conclusion and by the
new assumptions. The goal is an {eventually} statement about the state at step
{n-1}, and the tactic rewrites its conclusion into the same statement about the
state at step {n}, leaving a single subgoal. Every assumption mentioning the
old state — the program-counter, stack-pointer, register and flag readings, the
memory/events readings, the accumulated {MAYCHANGE} relation and the
loaded-bytes fact — is discharged and replaced by the corresponding assumption
about the new state, the {MAYCHANGE} relation being extended with the regions
the callee may write. Further assumptions characterising the event trace of the
call are added: the new {events} reading as an {APPEND} of a freshly introduced
trace variable {x1} onto the previous trace, an equation defining {x1} by the
callee's trace function applied to the call's concrete arguments, and a
memory-access-inbounds fact about {x1}. The assumption labelled {assump_name}
is removed from its position and re-added unchanged at the end of the
assumption list.

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this one kind of transformation, on goals of this
{eventually} form with a rich assumption context.

\ENDDOC
